cff-version: 1.2.0

message: >-
  If you use VOSS in academic work, please cite it using the metadata
  provided in this file.

title: >-
  VOSS: Vectorized Odd Segmented Sieve for Prime Gap Analysis

abstract: >-
  VOSS is a high-performance CUDA implementation for computing prime gaps
  using a Wheel-30 segmented sieve. It includes a complete mathematical
  verification pipeline (deterministic Miller-Rabin + Interval Sieve,
  SHA-256 signed certificates) and 12 statistical analyses with documented
  confidence levels. The project is verified against OEIS A006880 and the
  Prime Gap List Project up to 10^13.

